    "finding": "The HPA is accepted, targets the worker Deployment and reads real CPU. No scale event was observed. Worker CPU peaked at 76% of request for a single 15s sample during a burst and stayed at 8-34% under sustained load, because workers are dominated by waiting on the 500ms scheduler tick, database locks and Kafka rather than computing. CPU utilisation is therefore a weak scaling signal for this workload; durable READY queue depth would be a better one.",
